Added two multiplayer-server environment switches:

- `SERVER_DISABLE_TNT=true` — right-clicking TNT is inert; no explosion.
- `SERVER_DISABLE_LIQUID_FLOW=true` — water and lava no longer spread, fall, decay, or solidify on contact.

Accepted values are `true`, `1`, `yes`, and `on`; unset or any other value keeps normal behavior. The switches are read in [config.js](src/js/net/minecraft/server/config.js), enforced server-side through [World.js](src/js/net/minecraft/server/World.js), and checked by [BlockTNT.js](src/js/net/minecraft/client/world/block/type/BlockTNT.js) and [BlockLiquid.js](src/js/net/minecraft/client/world/block/type/BlockLiquid.js).

The server now sends its rules to clients on login and on `/server` switches, so local prediction does not explode TNT or start liquid flow when the server has disabled it. Settings are documented in [README.md](README.md) and left as commented examples in [docker-compose.yml](docker-compose.yml).

No tests were added or run. A syntax check and `npx vite build` both pass.
