**How it works**
- Find **Road Builder** in the Tools creative tab (golden shovel icon).
- Right-click the first spot to set the start. A translucent pavement preview appears while you aim.
- Right-click the second spot to build. Both points must share the same Y level and be in a straight line along X or Z.
- Mouse wheel changes road width, from 1 to 15.
- `R` cycles the road variant: **Black**, **White**, or **White Cracked**.
- Roads replace whatever blocks occupy the selected cells; the build is capped at 8,192 blocks.

