The loading screen now reports the active phase across singleplayer and multiplayer.

**What it shows**

- `Starting integrated server...` while the worker starts.
- `Loading world data...` while server/world data is read.
- `Connecting to world...` between integrated-server startup and the join handshake.
- `Loading textures...` when a texture pack is rebuilt.
- `Loading terrain...` while the client world is created and the chunk stream is pending.
- `Importing mods...` while server-sent mods are registered.
- `Building terrain...` once chunks are arriving/generating.
- `Respawning...` still appears on respawn, then switches to terrain building.

**Implementation**

- [GuiLoadingScreen.js](src/js/net/minecraft/client/gui/screens/GuiLoadingScreen.js) has a default title and safely ignores empty titles.
- [GuiLoadingIntegratedServer.js](src/js/net/minecraft/client/gui/screens/GuiLoadingIntegratedServer.js) has a dynamic status line instead of a fixed string.
- [Minecraft.js](src/js/net/minecraft/client/Minecraft.js) adds `setLoadingStatus()` and drives the singleplayer/world-creation phases.
- [NetworkManager.js](src/js/net/minecraft/client/network/NetworkManager.js) switches from mod import to terrain building after the server payload finishes.
- [ModLoader.js](src/js/net/minecraft/client/ModLoader.js) sets `Importing mods...` only after the world and atlas are ready, so texture loading is not mislabeled.
- Added Spanish and Hungarian translations for the new strings.

**Checks**

`npx vite build` passes. No live singleplayer/multiplayer session was run.

Local startup mods still load before the main menu, as before, so the status appears for mods sent when joining a world/server. The server-sent mod path is where the `Importing mods...` stage is visible.
