Implemented all three pieces.

### 1. Mod JSON storage

`ModAPI` now exposes per-mod persistent JSON:

```js
await ModAPI.saveJson('settings', { theme: 'dark' });
const settings = await ModAPI.loadJson('settings', {});
await ModAPI.deleteJson('settings');
const keys = await ModAPI.listJson();
```

Data is stored under `mod_data/<modId>/<key>.json`, not inside a read-only disk mod folder. Client and server-side mods both support it. Keys are validated to prevent path traversal.

### 2. Overlay text API

Mods can register a HUD provider that runs each frame:

```js
ModAPI.registerOverlayText((ctx) => {
    ctx.text('Hello from my mod', 10, 10, {
        color: '#55ff55',
        background: '#00000099',
        padding: 2,
        shadow: false
    });
});
```

The context also provides `ctx.measure(...)`, `ctx.rect(...)`, `ctx.width`, `ctx.height`, and the raw `ctx.stack`. Text supports newlines, alignment, scaling, and `§` color codes. It renders above the built-in HUD in [IngameOverlay.js](src/js/net/minecraft/client/gui/overlay/IngameOverlay.js).

### 3. Plots mod

Created [mods/plots/ModLoad.js](mods/plots/ModLoad.js) and [mods/plots/ModData.js](mods/plots/ModData.js).

Commands:

```text
/plot pos1
/plot pos2
/plot create <name> [radius]
/plot delete [name]
/plot rename <name>
/plot owner <player>
/plot trust <player>
/plot untrust <player>
/plot info
/plot list
/plot cancel
```

`create` uses the two selected corners when set; otherwise it creates a square around the player with a default radius of 16. Plots persist through `saveJson`, are synced to clients, and protect place/break/interact actions for anyone who is not the owner or a trusted member. The HUD shows:

```text
PlotName
Owner: PlayerName
```

in the top-left, offset below FPS/version text when those are enabled.

I also fixed server-side `ModAPI.registerCommand` so commands registered inside `ModLoad.onLoad` actually work on the authoritative server.

### Validation

- `npx vite build` passes.
- `git diff --check` passes.
- `node --check` passes for the plot mod, server mod loader, and data-key helper.
- Isolated server and client smoke runs verified plot creation, persistence, protection, sync, and HUD output.

No full live game session was run. A matching server-side copy is installed in [worlds/w_droptest_abcd/servermods/plots/ModLoad.js](worlds/w_droptest_abcd/servermods/plots/ModLoad.js) for the active world. `worlds/` is gitignored, so copy [mods/plots](mods/plots) into another world’s `servermods/` folder if you switch worlds.
