Plots are now chunk-based in [ModLoad.js](mods/plots/ModLoad.js).

What changed:

- Plot bounds are stored as `minChunkX/maxChunkX/minChunkZ/maxChunkZ`.
- `/plot pos1` and `/plot pos2` snap to the chunk containing the player and report both chunk and block coordinates.
- `/plot create` only creates whole-chunk rectangles, and the optional radius is now measured in chunks (`/plot create name 2` → a 5×5 chunk plot).
- Plot membership checks, overlap detection, and block-protection hooks compare chunk coordinates.
- `/plot info` shows chunk and block bounds; `/plot list` shows chunk ranges.
- Older block-based plot saves are migrated automatically by expanding their bounds outward to complete chunks.
- The size limit is now 16×16 chunks (256×256 blocks).

Validation: `node --check mods/plots/ModLoad.js` passes. No live world test was run.
